cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "explore_unizg: a prerequisite-graph course scheduler and an MCP server for the UNIZG course catalog"
message: "If you use this software or its data extraction approach, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pitlović
    given-names: Fabijan
    # email / affiliation / ORCID: add when finalizing
repository-code: "https://github.com/pitfa19/explore_unizg"
url: "https://horizontal-mobility.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Two tools for planning studies at the University of Zagreb. A browser app models a study
  programme as a prerequisite DAG and computes the earliest possible completion, respecting
  both prerequisite depth and the winter/summer season a course is taught in. An MCP server
  and Agent Skill give a language model read-only access to the ISVU public course catalog,
  covering all 37 UNIZG constituents and roughly 27,400 courses back to 1976/77, and can
  export a programme in the scheduler's import format.
keywords:
  - University of Zagreb
  - ISVU
  - course catalog
  - curriculum
  - prerequisite graph
  - directed acyclic graph
  - study planning
  - Model Context Protocol
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"
